WEBVTT

00:11.000 --> 00:15.450
(Episode 11: The Capital Distorted by the Twilight)

00:15.450 --> 00:16.980
(Episode 11: The Capital Distorted by the Twilight)
This is making me kind of nervous.

00:16.980 --> 00:17.680
This is making me kind of nervous.

00:17.680 --> 00:18.610
Same.

00:19.020 --> 00:22.610
But... I'm a little excited, too.

00:22.850 --> 00:23.960
Me, too!

00:25.030 --> 00:27.240
I hope we find something cool in here.

00:27.680 --> 00:31.380
Yeah. I'd be so happy to find
an undiscovered artifact.

00:31.380 --> 00:32.950
It's a new dungeon,

00:32.950 --> 00:36.050
so I wouldn't be surprised
if it held rare treasures.

00:36.050 --> 00:38.490
I'll hope for the best
without expecting too much.

00:38.490 --> 00:39.750
Gotta hold onto the dream.

00:39.750 --> 00:42.820
I hope there'll be some
dreams to find in here.

00:42.820 --> 00:44.510
I'm back!

00:45.180 --> 00:47.010
Welcome back. How'd it look?

00:47.010 --> 00:49.260
There was something in
there I didn't recognize!

00:49.680 --> 00:51.510
Something you didn't recognize?

00:55.810 --> 00:59.020
Well, I wonder what they'll find in there.

01:07.160 --> 01:14.120
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:32.410 --> 02:34.080
Are those chains?

02:34.080 --> 02:36.740
It's about the same height as an Orc.

02:36.740 --> 02:38.600
What do we do, Yuke?

02:39.510 --> 02:40.980
Let's launch an assault.

02:40.980 --> 02:41.870
Got it.

02:41.870 --> 02:42.560
Yeah.

02:44.040 --> 02:45.380
Physical Enchant!

02:45.630 --> 02:47.630
(Enhanced Stamina, Enhanced
Arm Strength, Enhanced Leg Strength)

02:47.630 --> 02:48.540
Let's go!

02:54.490 --> 02:56.760
Paralyze! Slow! Blindness!

02:57.020 --> 02:59.020
(Paralyze, Slow, Blindness)

03:02.770 --> 03:04.660
We're not doing much to it...

03:04.660 --> 03:06.900
Looks like it has some strong resistance.

03:12.350 --> 03:14.530
Venom! Collapse! Gravity!

03:14.780 --> 03:17.910
(Venom, Collapse, Gravity)

03:20.410 --> 03:22.780
Lightning, take its freedom away!

03:22.780 --> 03:23.290
Shock!

03:23.290 --> 03:25.040
(Shock)

03:25.040 --> 03:26.520
Magic Blade!

03:42.470 --> 03:44.580
What was that thing?

03:44.580 --> 03:46.910
Rain, Silk, what do you think?

03:47.520 --> 03:49.020
I don't know.

03:49.020 --> 03:49.980
You don't know?

03:50.450 --> 03:54.380
If I had to guess, I'd say it was
similar to a magical creature,

03:54.380 --> 03:56.120
but I sense impurity, too.

03:56.120 --> 03:59.990
I agree. It's like... something
undead with a life force.

04:00.500 --> 04:02.250
Like some kind of demon?

04:02.250 --> 04:06.130
Based on the spirits' unrest, that
seems like what it's closest to, but...

04:06.960 --> 04:09.770
But we don't know
what it actually is, huh?

04:09.770 --> 04:13.470
Let's have faith that the Royal Academy
scholars will be able to figure it out.

04:16.330 --> 04:19.620
There's something... weird...
inside the chains.

04:19.620 --> 04:20.770
Something weird?

04:21.070 --> 04:23.770
That tiny thing.

04:27.380 --> 04:28.910
A ring?

04:28.910 --> 04:32.140
It doesn't seem like it'd fit
on the Chain Man's finger.

04:32.140 --> 04:33.150
You're right.

04:33.560 --> 04:34.880
I'll appraise it.

04:38.130 --> 04:39.970
I can't tell much...

04:39.970 --> 04:42.900
It seems like some kind of
magic is imbued in it, but...

04:42.900 --> 04:45.420
I don't like the vibe coming from it.

04:45.420 --> 04:48.170
We'll have the scholars
check this out, too.

04:48.170 --> 04:49.800
What should we do?

04:49.800 --> 04:52.890
It looks like we could follow
the tracks left by the chains.

04:52.890 --> 04:54.520
You're right.

04:54.520 --> 04:57.680
Let's see if we can find where
the Chain Man came from first.

04:58.120 --> 04:59.180
I'm going in.

05:00.920 --> 05:03.060
That thing was pretty strong.

05:03.060 --> 05:06.360
If that's the kind of monster
that lives on the first floor,

05:06.360 --> 05:09.190
this might be a pretty tough dungeon.

05:09.760 --> 05:12.820
Hey, Yuke... Can I say something, too?

05:12.820 --> 05:16.930
I think, um... that thing was a human.

05:16.930 --> 05:18.390
Human?

05:18.390 --> 05:21.930
Yeah. I think it's an ability
of the Samurai job.

05:21.930 --> 05:25.580
I just... sort of know what
the things I kill are.

05:25.960 --> 05:27.180
I see...

05:27.180 --> 05:29.270
I think Marina's right.

05:29.270 --> 05:31.460
I mean, there's no magic gem.

05:31.930 --> 05:35.210
Maybe it's some sort of
demonic possession.

05:35.640 --> 05:37.090
I'm back!

05:37.430 --> 05:38.970
Two things to report.

05:38.970 --> 05:40.780
First, I found the stairway.

05:40.780 --> 05:42.060
Nice work, Nene.

05:42.060 --> 05:44.180
But... it leads up.

05:44.180 --> 05:45.500
Up?

05:45.500 --> 05:50.040
I would've expected it to lead
down, where the water goes...

05:50.040 --> 05:52.690
If it goes up, wouldn't that
take us back to the surface?

05:52.690 --> 05:56.820
And the second:
I found the Chain Man's nest.

06:03.000 --> 06:05.080
It doesn't look like a monster's nest.

06:05.660 --> 06:09.080
It's more like a break room and supply
closet for a waterway supervisor.

06:09.900 --> 06:11.580
There's something that looks like a book.

06:13.640 --> 06:14.840
Rain, you're up.

06:14.840 --> 06:15.710
Right.

06:16.050 --> 06:18.330
Reveal the evil scheme.

06:18.330 --> 06:20.220
Curse Sense.

06:22.280 --> 06:25.970
It seems safe. There's no curse on it.

06:27.830 --> 06:30.700
Looks like some type of
journal or memo book.

06:30.700 --> 06:31.800
You can read it?

06:31.800 --> 06:34.480
Nope. What language could this be?

06:35.210 --> 06:37.110
Could you decipher this, too, please?

06:37.110 --> 06:40.110
I don't see anything else that stands out.

06:40.710 --> 06:44.080
I hope this journal gives
us some kind of clue.

06:44.080 --> 06:45.610
What should we do, Yuke?

06:45.610 --> 06:47.510
Head for the stairs?

06:47.510 --> 06:50.620
Yeah. We'll have a meeting
there while we take a break.

06:52.330 --> 06:53.630
It's so bright.

06:53.630 --> 06:56.020
Maybe it really does lead outside?

06:56.020 --> 06:58.260
Based on the color, it looks like evening.

07:03.210 --> 07:04.430
Yuke!

07:04.430 --> 07:05.480
Are you all right?!

07:05.480 --> 07:06.090
Master!

07:06.090 --> 07:07.060
What's wrong?!

07:07.400 --> 07:11.020
Yeah... Sorry about that. I'm okay.

07:11.020 --> 07:13.560
Let's review our losses and take a break.

07:14.050 --> 07:15.180
Cut the stream.

07:15.180 --> 07:16.570
Goodnight.

07:26.120 --> 07:27.050
Rain?

07:27.050 --> 07:29.050
Just rest until you've calmed down.

07:29.050 --> 07:31.830
Don't hide your suffering. Okay?

07:32.330 --> 07:35.590
Thanks. I'll just rest a bit.

07:50.520 --> 07:53.470
Sorry. I'm okay now. Thanks.

07:54.020 --> 07:56.220
Hey, you scared us.

07:56.220 --> 07:57.770
Don't push yourself too hard.

07:58.120 --> 08:01.530
Yeah, it's just... This light...

08:01.940 --> 08:06.230
It's the same color the sky
was when I fought Simon.

08:06.230 --> 08:08.030
It just brought back a bit of trauma.

08:10.610 --> 08:11.880
Don't worry!

08:11.880 --> 08:16.660
Really, the color of the light just
triggered me more than I expected.

08:17.140 --> 08:18.170
H-Hey...

08:18.170 --> 08:21.170
I had no idea you were
struggling with it so much!

08:21.480 --> 08:23.930
Why didn't you tell us?

08:24.260 --> 08:25.550
We're your friends!

08:26.400 --> 08:30.560
Sorry. It's not because I don't
trust you guys or anything.

08:31.000 --> 08:36.690
I just felt like I needed to
deal with what I did on my own.

08:36.980 --> 08:38.840
Master, that's...

08:38.840 --> 08:41.690
I know. I was wrong.

08:41.690 --> 08:44.660
Talking about it now
helped me feel better.

08:46.200 --> 08:49.950
Next time, just talk to us, okay, Yuke?

08:49.950 --> 08:53.790
Master, please make sure
you tell me these things, too.

08:53.790 --> 08:54.930
Promise me.

08:54.930 --> 08:56.170
Me, too!

08:56.420 --> 08:57.970
I'll do that.

08:57.970 --> 08:59.420
Rain, same to you, of course.

08:59.760 --> 09:00.680
Yeah.

09:00.680 --> 09:03.550
Anyway, now that we've calmed
down, let's have our meeting.

09:03.960 --> 09:05.800
Should we continue to
explore the first floor

09:06.120 --> 09:07.800
or head up to the next floor?

09:07.800 --> 09:10.310
I think we should check out
what's upstairs!

09:10.310 --> 09:11.430
Me, too.

09:11.850 --> 09:13.440
I think I agree.

09:13.440 --> 09:16.310
It seems a bit different
from other dungeons.

09:16.870 --> 09:19.010
I'm of the same opinion.

09:19.010 --> 09:23.690
I can sense the environmental mana and
spirits in disarray beyond this stairway.

09:23.690 --> 09:25.720
Okay, then, it's settled.

09:25.720 --> 09:27.420
But first, let's eat!

09:27.420 --> 09:28.200
Right!

09:31.830 --> 09:32.950
Sel?

09:32.950 --> 09:34.200
Came!

09:35.720 --> 09:37.930
You borrowed it from Jamie?

09:37.930 --> 09:38.810
Yeah!

09:38.810 --> 09:43.090
We gotta keep our dungeon cooking streams
separate from the mission streams.

09:43.530 --> 09:46.070
It's what you call TPO!

09:46.070 --> 09:46.970
Makes sense.

09:47.240 --> 09:49.490
I actually practiced, too!

09:49.490 --> 09:50.720
Begin streaming!

09:50.720 --> 09:52.970
Understood.

09:55.730 --> 09:58.050
What's today's soup going to be?

09:58.050 --> 09:59.410
Let's see...

10:03.610 --> 10:05.460
It's meat soup!

10:05.460 --> 10:07.020
I love meat!

10:09.060 --> 10:11.870
Okay, looks good. Now we just...

10:14.870 --> 10:16.850
It's herb-steamed chicken.

10:16.850 --> 10:20.230
Your cooking skills get better
and better every time I see them.

10:20.230 --> 10:24.630
Feeding you guys tasty meals
is part of my support role.

10:25.700 --> 10:26.880
Okay, eat up.

10:26.880 --> 10:29.020
There's enough stew and bread for seconds.

10:29.020 --> 10:31.330
It looks amazing!

10:31.330 --> 10:32.890
Let's eat!

10:34.140 --> 10:36.020
It's so good!

10:40.750 --> 10:41.770
Oh my.

10:41.770 --> 10:45.800
Marina, this is all showing
up in your stream, you know.

10:46.280 --> 10:48.940
I'm in heaven!

10:56.270 --> 10:57.330
This is...

11:00.870 --> 11:03.580
It's... not Duna, is it?

11:03.580 --> 11:05.840
Duna doesn't have a castle.

11:06.210 --> 11:08.150
There's no one around.

11:08.150 --> 11:09.840
Is this a city-type dungeon?

11:10.320 --> 11:12.690
It doesn't look like a ruin.

11:12.690 --> 11:16.310
The buildings and cobblestone
all seem well-maintained.

11:16.600 --> 11:19.250
What should we do, Yuke?

11:19.250 --> 11:20.060
Let's turn back.

11:20.760 --> 11:24.380
We should discuss this with the
guild master and the Royal Academy.

11:24.380 --> 11:25.940
This place is too strange.

11:25.940 --> 11:29.320
Your perception is indeed correct.

11:29.320 --> 11:30.320
Heads up!

11:31.700 --> 11:32.820
Yuke, over there!

11:37.180 --> 11:38.080
Who are you?!

11:38.530 --> 11:40.520
I do beg your pardon.

11:40.520 --> 11:42.270
I am Loge,

11:42.270 --> 11:47.840
a poor old man who was left
behind in this broken world.

11:47.840 --> 11:53.000
Traveler, might I ask your name?

11:53.000 --> 11:56.100
I'm Yuke. Why are you in this dungeon?

11:56.100 --> 12:00.770
Oho! So this is the inside of a dungeon?

12:01.760 --> 12:04.740
The barrier truly is distorted!

12:04.740 --> 12:06.860
Wonderful!

12:07.230 --> 12:13.490
Travelers, allow me to introduce
you to my beautiful royal capital.

12:13.900 --> 12:20.620
This distorted city bathed in twilight's
glow is called Glad Shi-im.

12:20.620 --> 12:22.500
Glad Shi-im?

12:22.500 --> 12:24.680
I've never heard of that.

12:24.680 --> 12:29.150
It was once known as the "City of Joy,"

12:29.150 --> 12:32.510
but you can see for yourselves
what it has been reduced to.

12:32.840 --> 12:35.760
So are you the only one in this city?

12:35.760 --> 12:37.700
Certainly not.

12:37.700 --> 12:41.270
The king and the city's people
are here at this very moment.

12:41.270 --> 12:42.600
What do you mean?

12:43.020 --> 12:46.480
It is beyond my ability to explain.

12:46.970 --> 12:49.150
It would appear time is up.

12:49.150 --> 12:52.230
Farewell, traveler...

12:52.230 --> 12:54.740
Mr. Yuke Feldio.

12:55.560 --> 12:57.270
Until we meet again!

12:57.270 --> 12:57.990
Hey!

13:01.860 --> 13:04.130
I never told him my name was Feldio.

13:07.110 --> 13:09.000
There's Persephone's curse, too.

13:09.000 --> 13:10.770
This feels wrong.

13:10.770 --> 13:11.840
Let's hurry back!

13:12.280 --> 13:13.970
We'll take the shortest route!

13:13.970 --> 13:15.090
Wait!

13:15.090 --> 13:16.840
Someone's on the ground over there!

13:20.850 --> 13:22.120
(The Next Day)

13:22.120 --> 13:24.360
(The Next Day)
This has taken quite a strange turn.

13:24.360 --> 13:25.060
(The Next Day)
Yes.

13:25.720 --> 13:27.960
I can't believe the man who
introduced himself as Loge

13:27.960 --> 13:29.810
didn't show up in the stream.

13:30.150 --> 13:34.990
Perhaps you encountered some sort of
hallucination when you entered the square.

13:34.990 --> 13:37.320
That is the academy's conjecture.

13:37.780 --> 13:40.960
Well, I can't deny
that possibility, but...

13:40.960 --> 13:42.200
What about the ring?

13:42.200 --> 13:43.830
We're appraising it now.

13:43.830 --> 13:47.460
The same goes for the Chain Man
and the contents of the diary.

13:47.850 --> 13:52.520
In any case, we'll discuss what
to do about the mission here.

13:52.520 --> 13:53.460
Please do.

13:53.460 --> 13:57.220
Oh, also, Misty quit the mission.

13:57.220 --> 13:58.340
What?

13:58.340 --> 14:03.100
Apparently, half the members felt unwell
the moment they entered the dungeon.

14:05.540 --> 14:06.600
Tell me, son...

14:07.080 --> 14:09.200
What do you think that place is?

14:09.200 --> 14:11.980
I'm pretty sure I wrote
my thoughts in the log.

14:12.250 --> 14:15.730
I'm not asking for some
boring general opinion.

14:16.080 --> 14:18.350
What did you think of it?

14:20.030 --> 14:21.990
I think it might be an alternate world.

14:23.760 --> 14:26.150
Something felt just as off
as Achromatic Darkness did,

14:26.150 --> 14:28.420
if not more so.

14:28.420 --> 14:31.460
It felt as if we'd crossed
a border between worlds.

14:32.720 --> 14:35.460
Your inference is most likely correct.

14:35.460 --> 14:38.630
You really are just like Saga.

14:38.630 --> 14:42.000
I'll be relying on your intuition.

14:42.930 --> 14:45.470
You shouldn't expect too much of me.

14:45.750 --> 14:47.550
How's that girl?

14:47.550 --> 14:48.980
She's still asleep.

14:49.210 --> 14:52.820
All right.
Let me know if anything changes.

14:52.820 --> 14:53.480
I will.

14:58.780 --> 15:01.990
Could the condition of Misty's members
have to do with the twilight glow?

15:03.670 --> 15:07.720
There could be some sort of
magical effect in place there.

15:14.870 --> 15:15.910
I'm back.

15:19.400 --> 15:21.010
Rain, what is it?

15:22.060 --> 15:23.260
Count Crowder?

15:23.510 --> 15:26.770
Yes. My grandfather by blood,

15:26.770 --> 15:28.820
but essentially a stranger to me.

15:28.820 --> 15:30.890
You're a noble, Rain?

15:32.630 --> 15:34.750
I'm an illegitimate child.

15:34.750 --> 15:37.790
My mom was banished from
the count's household

15:37.790 --> 15:39.780
when she got pregnant with
the count's son's baby.

15:40.230 --> 15:42.730
Then she fell victim to a plague.

15:43.230 --> 15:46.530
I entered the magic academy
through a relative's connections

15:47.000 --> 15:48.700
and became an adventurer.

15:49.380 --> 15:53.330
But I never expected this
letter to come to me now.

15:56.820 --> 15:58.290
Is it all right if I look?

15:58.290 --> 15:59.460
No.

16:00.030 --> 16:01.470
But go ahead.

16:02.680 --> 16:05.400
"It has been decided what
will be done with you.

16:05.400 --> 16:09.990
His Highness Mastoma, Second Prince
of Salmutaria, has done us the honor

16:09.990 --> 16:11.350
of requesting your hand."

16:11.970 --> 16:13.350
What?!

16:15.090 --> 16:17.670
"You have never been of any use to us,

16:17.670 --> 16:20.810
and now the time has finally come for
you to be of use to the Crowder family."

16:20.810 --> 16:23.970
"You will cease working as a
crude, imprudent adventurer

16:23.970 --> 16:25.860
and return home at once."

16:25.860 --> 16:26.990
What is all this?!

16:27.600 --> 16:30.490
What do I do? I don't want...

16:30.920 --> 16:31.780
Rain...

16:32.370 --> 16:34.500
Wait, can't you just ignore it?

16:36.880 --> 16:39.190
You don't have to listen to this.

16:39.190 --> 16:42.620
I mean, it doesn't even have
your name anywhere on it.

16:42.620 --> 16:44.180
It went to the wrong person!

16:45.160 --> 16:47.010
Okay. We'll go with that.

16:47.550 --> 16:49.720
While doing business as a party,

16:49.720 --> 16:54.390
we received a letter that was
clearly some prank or mistake,

16:54.390 --> 16:56.020
and I accidentally lost it.

16:56.020 --> 17:00.000
After all, adventurers
are crude and imprudent.

17:00.000 --> 17:01.650
What can you do, right?

17:01.650 --> 17:03.000
Okay?

17:03.000 --> 17:04.650
Yuke...

17:06.120 --> 17:07.780
Letter? What letter?

17:07.780 --> 17:09.820
I never saw any letter.

17:09.820 --> 17:10.910
Same!

17:17.710 --> 17:22.580
We'll come up with a more reliable plan to
make sure the count doesn't get his way.

17:22.580 --> 17:23.320
Nene.

17:24.190 --> 17:27.230
Could you ask Mamar to get information on

17:27.230 --> 17:30.760
Count Crowder and the Second
Prince of Salmutaria?

17:30.760 --> 17:32.430
Huh? Mamar?

17:32.430 --> 17:37.300
And if there's any proof that Rain is
a daughter of the count's household,

17:37.300 --> 17:38.950
have her erase it all.

17:38.950 --> 17:40.240
But why?

17:40.240 --> 17:42.440
Mamar's just a receptionist, you know.

17:42.440 --> 17:45.190
You know how it is.
"Try the next window," right?

17:45.690 --> 17:47.720
I bet it's gonna cost you.

17:47.720 --> 17:49.570
I'll bring her some
really fancy souvenirs.

17:51.290 --> 17:52.670
Okay, got it.

17:52.670 --> 17:54.510
It's all to help Rain!

17:54.510 --> 17:56.040
Thanks. I appreciate it.

17:56.930 --> 17:59.210
I'm going to go see Maniella for a bit.

17:59.560 --> 18:02.200
You two start preparing for
our next dungeon assault.

18:02.200 --> 18:03.080
Understood.

18:03.080 --> 18:04.210
We're on it!

18:04.530 --> 18:06.040
Rain, you come with me.

18:06.040 --> 18:07.620
Oh... Okay.

18:10.100 --> 18:14.350
Listen, Rain. I'm about to try
something incredibly reckless.

18:15.100 --> 18:17.100
If you don't want to do it, say so.

18:17.440 --> 18:18.600
Reckless?

18:19.200 --> 18:20.600
Let's get married.

18:25.110 --> 18:27.740
Just temporarily, of course.

18:27.740 --> 18:30.990
I mean...
I hate to put it this way, but...

18:31.430 --> 18:33.920
I'll make you my property.

18:33.920 --> 18:35.990
I'd belong to you?

18:36.320 --> 18:38.370
You'll become an asset of mine,

18:38.370 --> 18:41.880
which means no Salmutarian
can mess with you.

18:42.260 --> 18:45.780
It should be a pretty effective
way to protect you.

18:48.450 --> 18:49.930
You don't want to, then?

18:52.920 --> 18:53.980
No, it's fine.

18:54.800 --> 18:56.970
Yeah. I want to do that.

18:58.270 --> 19:00.100
You don't need to worry about a thing.

19:00.440 --> 19:03.980
Yeah. I belong to you.

19:06.360 --> 19:08.680
Let's get married.

19:11.860 --> 19:13.210
(The Next Morning)

19:13.210 --> 19:14.620
(The Next Morning)
We've decided on a plan.

19:15.000 --> 19:17.170
We'll continue the investigation.

19:17.170 --> 19:20.120
We're down to two parties,
but give it your all.

19:20.470 --> 19:21.000
What happens to the mission?

19:21.000 --> 19:23.000
(Fullbound Leader, Zaccard)
What happens to the mission?

19:23.000 --> 19:26.520
It becomes an internal
location investigation.

19:26.520 --> 19:29.180
We'll continue to evaluate all of you,

19:29.180 --> 19:30.590
and the time frame is the same.

19:30.590 --> 19:33.010
Got it. We'll get right to it.

19:33.010 --> 19:34.010
So will we!

19:34.840 --> 19:39.890
Your little joke of a C-rank party
full of girls can just butt out!

19:39.890 --> 19:44.270
That A-rank promotion is
gonna be going to Fullbound!

19:49.700 --> 19:50.770
Yuke.

19:51.530 --> 19:52.360
Yes?

19:52.850 --> 19:55.120
Your marriage plan was approved.

19:55.560 --> 19:59.870
Even if it's only on paper,
that's quite a leap you took.

20:00.190 --> 20:02.790
We can't leave any room for confusion

20:02.790 --> 20:04.880
when dealing with nobles and Salmutarians.

20:06.050 --> 20:09.130
Is this really "only on paper," though?

20:13.850 --> 20:16.530
The goal of our second
assault in this dungeon

20:16.530 --> 20:20.520
is a location investigation of the
twilight capital, Glad Shi-im.

20:20.520 --> 20:24.300
We'll find out how big it is,
what kinds of monsters live there,

20:24.300 --> 20:26.340
and if possible, check out the castle.

20:26.340 --> 20:27.730
Let's have fun, but be careful!

20:32.000 --> 20:34.260
Master, are you all right?

20:34.260 --> 20:36.360
Thanks for asking. I'm fine.

20:36.360 --> 20:38.910
But doesn't it look brighter
than last time?

20:39.410 --> 20:42.870
Maybe it changes with the passage of time.

20:42.870 --> 20:45.250
We'll compare the footage
when we get back.

20:46.260 --> 20:50.250
You've seemed a little strange since
yesterday, Rain. Are you all right?

20:51.820 --> 20:54.120
Did something happen after you left?

20:54.120 --> 20:55.440
Did something happen?

20:56.240 --> 20:57.890
A dream happened.

20:57.890 --> 20:59.140
A dream?

20:59.140 --> 21:02.770
Anyway, time to get started! Let's focus!

21:03.290 --> 21:04.420
Uh-huh...

21:04.420 --> 21:05.140
Yeah.

21:05.540 --> 21:07.150
Let's do our best.

21:09.150 --> 21:12.080
Yuke! There's something in the square!

21:12.080 --> 21:14.530
I don't know if it's a monster or what!

21:21.130 --> 21:22.160
What...

21:22.160 --> 21:23.400
is that?!

22:55.920 --> 22:56.830
(The Golden Shrine Maiden)

22:56.830 --> 22:59.170
(The Golden Shrine Maiden)
Next time, "The Golden Shrine Maiden."

22:59.170 --> 23:00.930
(The Golden Shrine Maiden)
